(r"""Before any journey the traveller's OWN court plans on what it BELIEVES about the roads ahead: `believedWatch(worldState, snapshot, observerId, stretch, tick)` — its own riders' reports of the foreign town's riders (§9.3), its spies' products (ES), rumor — never the foreign town's truth. ONE read, consumed in each planner's commit (a registration, never a second planning law): ES's mission planning (the dispatch refusal already reads BELIEVED danger, ES HZ9), the errand spine's route, CH's leg choice, PT's reachability card (the DM's view of where the party could go unseen), EC-18's open road and WY's caravans (timing a departure, §6.3).""",
r"""Before any journey the traveller's OWN court plans on what it BELIEVES about the roads ahead: `believedWatch(worldState, snapshot, observerId, roadKey, tick)` — never the foreign town's truth. ITS PRODUCERS, named [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-16: the compiled read had no producer and an undefined `null`]: (1) its OWN riders at a shared gate see the neighbour's riders on the neighbour's half — a `patrol_report` with `finding: 'riders_seen'` (§9.3; PR's own producer); (2) its ALLIES' riders' reports, exchanged at the gate (§10.1(b)); (3) its TRAVELLERS' RETURN — a named traveller of its own that met (or did not meet) riders on a road carries the fact home on its owner's carried-picture idiom (the errand spine's envoy picture, RF-6; a caravan's factor) — one watched/unwatched row per road crossed, a registration in each owner's commit (PLAUSIBLE until each owner's car-0 measures its picture's room); (4) ES's PRODUCT — a spy at a foreign town reports the watch on its roads (ES's product row, ES's commit); (5) RUMOR of a clash or a catch on the road (a travelling `patrol_report`). Each belief ages toward the prior over the rumor's own TTL; with nothing heard the read returns the TIER-REFERENCE PRIOR of the road's holder with `known: false`, and the card says "unknown". ONE read, consumed in each planner's commit (a registration, never a second planning law): ES's mission planning (the dispatch refusal already reads BELIEVED danger, ES HZ9), the errand spine's route, CH's leg choice, EC-18's open road and WY's caravans (timing a departure, §6.3). PT does NOT consume it — the DM sees all, and PT's reachability card is the DM's read, not a court's belief (PT's own patrols line) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-24]."""),
